            "content": "MOSAIC Validation Runbook\nReference: MOSAIC-KB-20261031\nThis authored document is a control corpus for the Spark validation run.\nA vector(1) alert is a deliberate delivery-path test. It does not show a GPU, driver or application\nfault. Verify the Prometheus state, Alertmanager fingerprint and the same MOSAIC alert before\ninterpreting it.\nAn alert injected directly through the Alertmanager API bypasses Prometheus rule evaluation.\nMissing Prometheus ALERTS samples for that injected run ID are expected. Do not claim a new\nPrometheusRule was evaluated.\nFor an isolated user-level repair demo, the named service fails when its ready marker is absent.\nRead the exact service state and logs before repair. Repair only the registered demo wrapper;\nverify the marker and service result afterward.\nMOSAIC authored validation corpus | test from Jeff Peng 1",
